---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Herru Adi"
  description="I'm Herru Adi — a strategic design partner with 9+ years working across fintech, AI, SaaS, and enterprise products. I bring the kind of thinking that shapes what gets built — not just how it looks."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>

    <!-- ─── Page Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-20 pt-36 md:pb-24 md:pt-44">
      <p class="mb-5 font-mono text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">
        About
      </p>
      <h1 class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-[2.6rem] font-bold leading-[1.07] tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl">
        I'm not here to<br />
        execute your brief.
      </h1>
      <p class="max-w-xl text-lg leading-[1.8] text-muted">
        A strategic design partner who believes the best design decisions
        happen before any screen is made.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ─── Who I Am ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="who-i-am">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:gap-14 lg:gap-20">

          <!-- Left: photo placeholder, max 400px tall -->
          <div class="mb-24 w-full shrink-0 md:mb-0 md:w-[360px]">
            <div
              class="relative w-full overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-border bg-surface"
              style="aspect-ratio: 4/5; max-height: 400px;"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <!-- Ghost initials watermark -->
              <span
                class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 flex select-none items-center justify-center font-bold text-fg"
                style="font-size: 10rem; line-height: 1; opacity: 0.045;"
              >HA</span>

              <!-- Frosted name card -->
              <div class="absolute bottom-4 left-4 right-4">
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-bg/75 px-4 py-3 backdrop-blur-sm">
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-fg">Herru Adi</p>
                  <p class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-muted">Strategic Design Partner</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Right: label + prose -->
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col items-start justify-center">
            <div class="mb-7 inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-2.5 rounded-full border border-border bg-surface px-4 py-1.5">
              <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span
                id="who-i-am"
                class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted"
              >Who I Am</span>
            </div>

            <div class="text-[17px] sm:text-lg">
              <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
                I started as a frontend developer — close enough to design to fall in love
                with it, far enough to understand how things get built.
              </p>
              <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
                The switch wasn't planned. But once I crossed over, I never looked back.
              </p>
              <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
                Nine years later, what keeps me here isn't the craft — it's the impact.
                A product I designed helping a kitchen run smoother. An app that actually
                solves someone's real problem. An agency that lands a client because the
                work looked and felt right. Small ripples, maybe. But ripples matter.
              </p>
              <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
                I live by one principle:{' '}
                <span class="font-semibold text-fg">hidup harus berguna bagi sesama</span>
                {' '}— life should be useful to others. It's why I design, why I'm honest
                with clients even when it's uncomfortable, and why I named my son Gunaka
                Sasama — Sundanese for "useful to others."
              </p>
              <p class="leading-[1.8] font-bold text-fg">
                That's not a tagline. That's just who I am.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── How I Work ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="how-i-work">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">

        <div class="mb-8 inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-2.5 rounded-full border border-border bg-surface px-4 py-1.5">
          <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span
            id="how-i-work"
            class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted"
          >How I Work</span>
        </div>

        <div class="max-w-[65ch] text-[17px] sm:text-lg">
          <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] font-bold text-fg">
            My process starts with one question: is this actually the problem?
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
            Before I open Figma, I want to understand what we're really solving.
            I break down the problem, challenge the assumptions, and make sure we're
            building the right thing — not just building things right. If something
            doesn't make sense, we talk it through. Designing the wrong solution is
            just expensive guesswork.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] font-bold text-fg">
            That said — I know when to lead and when to follow.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
            When there's a PM or PO with a solid PRD on the table, I'm heads down
            and executing with precision. I respect process, I respect structure,
            and I know how to work within a system without losing the quality of
            the output.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-[1.8] font-bold text-fg">
            Two modes. One standard: make it count.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── The Human Side ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-24" aria-labelledby="human-side">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">

        <div class="mb-8 inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-2.5 rounded-full border border-border bg-surface px-4 py-1.5">
          <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span
            id="human-side"
            class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted"
          >The Human Side</span>
        </div>

        <div class="max-w-[65ch] text-[17px] sm:text-lg">
          <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
            Outside of work, I'm a dad who does the school run every morning for
            my 4-year-old — which, honestly, is the best part of my day.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-6 leading-[1.8] text-muted">
            I decompress on two wheels, exploring Bandung's streets or finding
            roads I've never taken before. I keep telling myself I'll pick up
            music again soon.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-[1.8] text-muted">
            The bigger dream? A design studio and a free learning space for people
            who want to build in tech but can't afford the privilege of education.
            Not someday — just not today yet.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactCTA />

  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
